#: ../../index.rst:4
msgid "**Write once. Explain well. Publish on the web and on paper.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:6
msgid "Guidedog is a documentation generator. It builds HTML websites and PDF books from reStructuredText and Markdown sources. It is one self-contained program, written in Rust. It needs no Python environment and no LaTeX installation. The conversion engine is called **Guidedoc**. The embedded Typst compiler typesets the PDF pages, and Guidedog writes the website directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:12
msgid "A small project needs three things: a source document, a table of contents, and ``conf.toml``. Start with :doc:`tutorial/first-project`. For a particular task, use :doc:`howto/index`. For an exact contract, use :doc:`reference/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:19
msgid "RST and Markdown enter Guidedoc; HTML goes to a browser and Typst produces PDF."
msgstr ""

